.TH MRSTREAM 1 "2026-07-12" "0.1.0-alpha" "MrStream-Cli Manual"
.SH NAME
mrstream \- terminal-based sports event browser and stream launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mrstream
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
MrStream-Cli is a minimalist, terminal-native sports event browser and stream
launcher. It fetches live sports schedules, lets you search and select events
via an interactive \fBfzf\fR menu, then resolves and plays the stream in your
preferred video player.

This tool is NOT affiliated with sportsonline.st, sportsonline.vc,
sportssonline.click, or any content provider.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search \fI"query"\fR
Search for sports events. Shows all events if no query is given, or filters
by the provided search term.
.TP
.B doctor
Check that all required dependencies are installed and report any missing ones.
.TP
.B update
Self-update from the git repository. Pulls the latest changes and reinstalls
if the tool was installed via the install script.
.TP
.B version
Display the current version string.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Force a refresh of the local cache, ignoring cached results.
.TP
.B \-\-download
Download the selected stream to disk instead of playing it. Uses
\fByt-dlp\fR if available, then falls back to \fBffmpeg\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-quality \fIQUALITY\fR
Set preferred stream quality. Accepts values like \fB1080p\fR, \fB720p\fR,
\fBbest\fR, or \fBworst\fR. When set, variant playlists are parsed and
the matching quality is selected automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable resolver debug output. Prints diagnostic information during stream
resolution.
.TP
.B \-\-player \fIPLAYER\fR
Force a specific video player. Supported: \fBmpv\fR, \fBvlc\fR, \fBcvlc\fR,
\fBmplayer\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display the help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MRSTREAM_PLAYER
Set the default video player (e.g., \fBMRSTREAM_PLAYER=vlc\fR).
.TP
.B MRSTREAM_QUALITY
Set the preferred stream quality (e.g., \fBMRSTREAM_QUALITY=720p\fR).
.TP
.B MRSTREAM_DOWNLOAD_DIR
Set the download directory (default: \fB~/Downloads\fR).
.TP
.B DEBUG
Enable debug output when set to 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Browse all available events:
.B mrstream search
.TP
Search for specific events:
.B mrstream search "UFC"
.TP
Force cache refresh and search:
.B mrstream \-\-refresh search
.TP
Download a stream instead of playing:
.B mrstream \-\-download search
.TP
Select a specific quality:
.B mrstream \-\-quality 1080p search
.TP
Update to the latest version:
.B mrstream update
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mrstream/sources.yaml
Configuration file for enabling external sources and acknowledging
non-affiliation disclaimers.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mrstream/*.cache
Cache directory for fetched schedules (1-hour TTL).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B curl
For fetching data from remote sources.
.TP
.B fzf
For the interactive search and selection menu.
.TP
.B mpv
Recommended video player for stream playback.
.TP
.B yt-dlp\fR/\fBffmpeg
Optional: for downloading streams (used by \fB\-\-download\fR).
.TP
.B git
Required for the \fBupdate\fR command.
